  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that if a plane passes through the line of intersection of planes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;then the family of planes is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>.</p><p>Equation of plane after rotation :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now angle between the new plane and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Equation of plane :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Distance of plane from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>26</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>54</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mn>54</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>54</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>126</mn></math></p><p>Hence this is the required option.</p>",
